TI  - Effect of aerobic pretreatment of waste on the rate of anaerobic treatment processes
AU  - Suchowska-Kisielewicz, Monika
AU  - Jedrczak, Andrzej
AU  - Sadecka, Zofia
AU  - Myszograj, Sylwia
PY  - 2013
JO  - Journal of Material Cycles and Waste Management
VL  - 15
IS  - 2
DO  - 10.1007/s10163-012-0100-y
AB  - The efficiency of waste degradation can be expressed by the rate of waste decomposition in individual phases. This article presents the durations of degradation phases of pretreated and untreated waste stabilized in anaerobic laboratory reactors. In this investigation, the quantities of organic and nitrogen contaminants emitted from the waste during the study are presented. The study confirmed the beneficial effects of aerobic pretreatment of waste before landfilling on reducing the duration of hydrolysis and acid phases, and speeding up the start of the stable methane phase. In the pretreated waste reactor, the stable methane phase began about 19 weeks earlier than in the untreated waste. The total amounts of contaminants removed from the aerobic pretreatment waste were lower than from untreated waste, with values of COD, TOC, BOD 5 , and VFA corresponding to 21, 18, 6, and 23 %, respectively, and values of TKN and NH 4 of 7 and 50 %, respectively.
